[36m(TaskRunner pid=3717577)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3717577)[0m We need \( b + 7 \) to be a divisor of \( 9b + 7 \). So, we can write:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3717577)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3717577)[0m for some integer \( k \). Rearranging this equation, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3717577)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = kb + 7k \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3717577)[0m \[ 9b - kb = 7k - 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3717577)[0m \[ b(9 - k) = 7(k - 1) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3717577)[0m \[ b = \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3717577)[0m For \( b \) to be an integer, \( \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \) must be an integer. This means that \( 9 - k \) must be a divisor of \( 7(k - 1) \). Let's find the possible values of \( k \) by checking the divisors of \( 7(k - 1) \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3717577)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3717577)[0m The possible values for \( 9 - k \) are the divisors of \( 7(k - 1) \). Since \( b > 9 \), \( k \) must be less than 9. Let's check the possible values for \( k \):
