[36m(TaskRunner pid=3739292)[0m [response] To solve the equation \(2^8 = 4^x\), we can express both sides of the equation with the same base. We know that \(4\) can be written as \(2^2\), so we can rewrite the equation as follows:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3739292)[0m 
