[36m(TaskRunner pid=3739292)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3739292)[0m Given that \(N\) and \(a_k\) are congruent modulo \(k\) for each \(k = 1, 2, \ldots, 20\), we can deduce the following:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3739292)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3739292)[0m 1. \(N \equiv a_1 \pmod{1}\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3739292)[0m 2. \(N \equiv a_2 \pmod{2}\)
