[36m(TaskRunner pid=3739292)[0m 4. \(\vdots\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3739292)[0m 5. \(N \equiv a_{20} \pmod{20}\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3739292)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3739292)[0m Since \(N\) is a positive integer not exceeding 5000, we can use the Chinese Remainder Theorem (CRT) to find \(N\) uniquely if we know the values of \(a_k \mod k\) for \(k = 1, 2, \ldots, 20\). However, since we don't know the exact values of \(a_k\), we need to determine the minimum number of moves required to uniquely identify \(N\).
